########## 05_null_resolution ##########
[1] B = 200 ; p floor = 1/(B+1) = 0.00498 ; (prototype cap B=100 -> 0.00990)
[2] naive (distinct-p) bound m <= alpha*(B+1) = 10.1 would block 32 of 134 productive cells;
    but 32 of those actually DO produce significant regions, because their p-values
    are tied at the floor and BH rejects tied sets together.
[2] tie-aware condition (p0 <= alpha*k/m) predicts the cell's outcome correctly in 100 of 134 cells
    -> the operative driver of per-cell significance is the FRACTION of regions at the
       p-value floor (median 0.29, range 0.00-0.67), i.e. how many regions the null
       fails to rebuild AT ALL -- not the strength of any individual region.
[2] a cell where EVERY region is at the floor rejects every one of them: 0 such cells
    lmin cells m_median m_max median_frac_floor cells_with_sig
